version: "2.0"
description: >-
  Gnomon contracts — versioned TS types, hand-written zero-dependency
  validators and JSON Schemas for the Gnomon kernel's hard contracts
  (docs/specs/gnomon.md §4, §5, §9.1, §12.8, §18). Zero runtime deps and zero
  imports (the kernel bundles it; platform-neutral, WebCrypto getRandomValues
  only). Contracts change additively or with a version bump (§4.9). PR-0
  shipped probeResult:v1; PR-3 (research 29 §4) adds event:v1, ids/hsid,
  principals, ref:v1, refusal:v1, card:v1, the gnomon-rpc:v1 hello shape and
  the frozen client surface, with the P8-D58 (voice) and P8-R9 (linking)
  values reserved for M1.1. M1.1 part 2 (spec v3.9 §4.11, §19.1 M1.1) reserves
  the P8-D86–D88 values (strictness L0–L3, run modes, review convergence,
  change notes) and adds review-finding:v1 and change-note:v1, moving
  clientApiId once now so it does not move in Move 2; no closed enumeration
  (refusal code, retriable, audience, sensitivity) gains a value. Spec Appendix A names no contract-level nodes, so
  every component below is a child of #gnomon-contracts named after the
  contract id it implements; the spec owners it serves are #identity,
  #kernel-log, #ref-resolver, #approval-broker, #socket, #peer-link and
  ~ample-internal-logs (all in packages/gnomon). Gates it encodes values for:
  ^voice-armed (§14.7), ^peer-paired (§3.9), ^certified (§7.3 review cap). The spec declares no signals.
  Private, Node >= 24, outside the root build until the 8.0 cut.

components:
  gnomon-contracts:
    description: >-
      Package entry (src/index.ts, re-exports every module) plus schemas/.
      probeResult:v1 = {probe, os, osVersion, arch, toolVersions{node,...},
      verdict pass|fail|partial, evidence{}, specRefs[], at};
      schemas/probeResult.v1.schema.json is its JSON Schema, src/probe-result.ts
      the TS type plus validateProbeResultV1 / isProbeResultV1. The PR-3
      schemas in schemas/ are GENERATED from src/schemas.ts
      (`npm run schemas`, scripts/write-schemas.mjs) and a test keeps them a
      byte-identical fixed point. src/internal.ts holds the shared pure helpers
      (Checker with strict|tolerant modes, UTF-8, synchronous SHA-256,
      Crockford base32, canonical JSON, deepFreeze). Also home (no allowlisted
      sub-component yet; spec Appendix A has no node) of the M1.1-reserved
      (P8-D86–D88, §4.11) schemas: src/change-note.ts = change-note:v1 —
      agentClaims{testedHow{summary ≤1 KiB, refs[]}, risk{tier low|medium|high,
      why ≤512 B, blast[sym:]}, revert{how auto|command|manual, steps ≤1 KiB
      never executed, reversible}, draftedBy} UNTRUSTED and kept structurally
      apart from kernel{verified{n, of}, risk{floor, effective, reasons[]},
      revert{how auto|none, ref?}} (B16); validateChangeNoteV1 needs an explicit
      form (no default): claim (contract.claim{note}: agentClaims only, a
      kernel part refused in every mode) or card (kernel required; strict:
      effective = max(floor, agent tier)); schemas/change-note.v1.schema.json
      publishes both as $defs/claim (kernel: false) and $defs/card, with
      x-gnomon-trust per part; failSafe* readings and changeNoteHasUnknownValue.
      src/review-finding.ts = review-finding:v1 {fid, round >= 1, class,
      severity important|nit|pre-existing (kernel-set), locus{path, lines?,
      symbol?}, instances[], claim, fingerprint}; `lines` = "n" or "from-to"
      (spec gives no grammar; judgment call); FINDING_RESPONSES fixed|wrong|
      intentional|immaterial + validateFindingResponses for
      contract.claim{responses}; schemas/review-finding.v1.schema.json. Tiers,
      hows, severities and responses are ADDITIVE with fail-safe readings
      (unknown tier ⇒ high, agent revert how ⇒ manual, kernel revert how ⇒
      none, severity ⇒ important, response ⇒ no answer; round-2 ruling). They serve #approval-broker and ^certified convergence.
      M1.12 slice 1 (§4.5, §4.9, §9.1, §12.8), additive and NOT inputs to
      clientApiId (pin unchanged): src/display.ts = sanitizeDisplayText (the
      client-side §4.5 rules as amended by Aegis round 2 and M1.12 slice 2:
      a terminated OSC/DCS/SOS/PM/APC shown as ⟨OSC⟩payload⟨ST⟩ (payload
      visible, Aegis M2), CSI and other ESC sequences removed, an
      unterminated ESC shown as ⟨ESC⟩ with its tail visible; zero-width, tag,
      VS-supplement and filler characters stripped, misplaced U+FE00–FE0F
      (decided on the output, never after a mark) stripped, a kept
      U+FE00–FE0D flagged (only VS15/VS16 silent), U+2028/2029 ⇒ \n, all ⇒
      hidden-chars; bidi controls and marks ⇒ visible glyphs ⇒ bidi; remaining
      C0/C1 removed ⇒ hidden-chars, CR unflagged; lone surrogates ⇒ U+FFFD; no
      normalisation; text idempotent, flags idempotent except that a kept
      U+FE00–FE0D re-flags hidden-chars; display.v1.json normative), eventRow (opaque
      {kind, principal, at} rows for modns.* and kinds newer than the
      package), renderDenominator ({n, of} or refused); src/conformance.ts =
      the conformance catalog (CONFORMANCE_CHECKS, run vs slice-2), the
      display vectors (conformance/display.v1.json, generated by
      `npm run conformance`, fixed point) and conformanceReportHash;
      src/client-types.ts = TYPE-ONLY params/results of the 12 verbs + 2 relays.
      M1.12 slice 3: src/client-api-doc.ts = renderClientApiDoc(), a pure
      render of the published surface (ids, verbs + access, relays, refusal
      codes + reasons, additive enums, kinds, schema files, kit, sanitizer
      sets, conformance catalog) into docs/specs/gnomon-client-api.md —
      generated by `npm run client-api-doc`, never hand-maintained; the
      committed file is its byte-identical fixed point (G-HON-04 rule, LF on
      every OS via .gitattributes); not an input to clientApiId (pin unchanged).
    path: src/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, json-schema, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/probe-result.test.ts
      - test/contracts.test.ts
      - test/m1-1-reservations.test.ts
      - test/client-api-doc.test.ts

  contract-event-v1:
    description: >-
      event:v1 envelope (§4.1) — P8-D98 (T-2026-10-19-001): reserves, tag
      8.0:P8-D98, session.drained{uuid, reason} (DRAIN_REASONS = [upgrade],
      closed), permit.reattributed{permitId, hsid, drainedEventId,
      renewedByDrain:true, expiresAt} (founder carry-over ruling: a permit live
      at the drain gets a fresh window, never minted),
      approval.rule.revoked{ruleId, repoKey, tool, connId} and
      approval.effect.failed{cardId, decision, effect, reason}, each with a
      closed payload check (validateKindPayload; an extra field is refused, an
      unchecked kind is an error); reserved payload fields contract.claimed
      claimGen, approval.rule.learned match (ALWAYS_RULE_MATCHES = [exact],
      validateAlwaysRuleMatch, TD-2026-10-19-528 F2) and approval.expire why.
      Drain-and-resume (T-2026-10-19-014 B1/B2, Aegis M1 G-HON): reserved
      session.open resume{drainedEventId, outcome} + principalClass,
      session.sandbox resumedFrom/drainOutcome/note/drainedEventId,
      session.inject deadlineMs/deadlineSource/failed, session.refused resume;
      closed sets DRAIN_OUTCOMES, DRAIN_EXIT_REASONS [drain-clean,
      drain-interrupted], DRAIN_INJECT_CHANNELS [drain],
      DRAIN_DEADLINE_SOURCES, SANDBOX_D98_PHASES [resume-note], RESUME_NOTES,
      RESUME_REFUSALS — all in D98_CLOSED_VALUES.
      P8-D93 (T-2026-10-18-016): kernel-owned
      session.compacted{hsid, turn, reason, summaryHash, tokensBefore,
      tokensAfter} (summaryHash a sensitive field), KIND_PAYLOADS (published as
      x-gnomon-kind-payloads) and validateSessionCompactedPayload. P8-D89
      (M1.4): reserves daemon.log.quarantined
      (evidencePath a sensitive field) and adds key.token.revoked{tokenId},
      tag M1.4:P8-D89. EventV1 type, validateEventV1/isEventV1
      (strict = registered kind + closed fields; tolerant = unknown kinds and
      fields accepted, opaqueEventView renders {kind, principal, at}),
      schemas/event.v1.schema.json. The kind registry EVENT_KINDS (§9.1,
      owner kernel|userland, M1.1 reservations tagged M1.1:P8-D58 /
      M1.1:P8-R9 / M1.1:P8-D86-D88 — the last: approval.strictness.raised|
      proposed|lowered|held, approval.mode.set, approval.auto,
      contract.review.returned|capped|extended|restarted, merge.reverted,
      merge.ref.rewritten, verdict.incident, request.strictness.set|mode.set|
      incident, all kernel-owned, private + normal) with RESERVED_PAYLOAD_FIELDS
      (oracle.result round/range/findings, contract.knot reopenOf,
      contract.built note/responses, verdict.founder override, session.inject
      briefId/peerRootKeyId, session.tainted taint), SESSION_TAINTS and
      APPROVAL_SUSPECT_REASONS (voice-* and strictness-class), and per-kind default labels: audience private, sensitivity
      per §9.1 (session.inject, turn.event, voice.turn.* sensitive; voice.enrol
      secret; field labels approval.request.tool_input and oracle.result.evidence
      sensitive). defaultLabelsFor(kind) returns undefined for an unregistered
      kind so the kernel refuses rather than guesses (S32 §6, L6, G-LOG-09
      contract half). Serves #kernel-log and ~ample-internal-logs.
    path: src/event.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, event-v1, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/contracts.test.ts
      - test/m1-1-reservations.test.ts

  contract-project-hue:
    description: >-
      The ONE project-hue function (critique 2026-10-20 S2.1): projectHue(key)
      = sha256(utf8(key))[0] mod PROJECT_HUES (6), the six pigments of
      design-system.yaml gnomon.colour. The kernel's Workshop feed
      (modhost/feed.ts session.open project) and the GUI's sessions rail both
      call it with the session.open cwd, so a project never gets two hues. A
      project hue is identity only, never state. Pure (in-house sha256), so it
      runs in the browser bundle too.
    path: src/hue.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, gui, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/hue.test.ts
  contract-workshop-cap:
    description: >-
      The Workshop cap (critique 2026-10-20 S5.3): a closed, minimal shape a
      mod may put on a kit Text node, {shape tall|wide|floppy, hue
      0..PROJECT_HUES-1, filled bool, state needs|working|idle|knot, label
      1..40 code points, one line}. checkCap refuses any unknown, missing,
      mistyped or out-of-range field and returns a fresh five-key object. The
      kernel mod-block gate (modhost/block.ts) and the GUI renderer both call
      it; a client draws the hat from these fields only (no mod SVG, path,
      colour or attribute). Not an input to kitId, modAbiId or clientApiId.
    path: src/cap.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, gui, workshop, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/cap.test.ts
  contract-ids:
    description: >-
      Ids (§4.2, §3.1, S32-13) — ULID (ulid, monotonicUlidFactory with
      in-ms increment and overflow refusal, isUlid, ulidTime) over
      globalThis.crypto.getRandomValues; prefixed ULID ids ev/log/conn/card/arm/
      permit:v1/brief/msg/ds (mintId, isId); hsid:v1 (mintHsid, non-monotonic so
      hsid-short stays fully random), hsid:v1d derivation (deriveHsidV1d),
      hsid-short = lowercase Crockford of the ULID's 80 random bits, 16 chars
      (hsidShort); turn ids turn:<hsid>/<n> (turnId, parseTurnId); keyId,
      repo-scope and contract-id patterns. Serves #identity.
    path: src/ids.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, ids, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/ids-principal-ref.test.ts

  contract-principal:
    description: >-
      Principals (§3.1, S32-02, P8-D75) — PRINCIPAL_KINDS human|agent|session|
      kernel|mod|voice|peer; p:<ns>/<name> and the foreign display form
      p:<ns>/<name>@<rootKeyId8> (parsePrincipalId marks it foreign, never
      local); samePrincipal compares full rootKeyId + name and never ns;
      isLocalPrincipal, foreignDisplayId, nsFromRootPublicKey,
      peerKernelPrincipal. Also the closed-kind row vocabularies of §3.1/§15.4:
      REGISTRY_ROW_KINDS (kernel, link), GRANT_ROW_KINDS (incl. reserved
      grant.voice-approvals, grant.peer), CAPABILITY_FORMS (incl. log.read:usage, the #mod-host usage feed grant, Aegis M1) and
      FIRST_PARTY_ONLY_CAPABILITIES (link:send, knowledge:federate),
      GRANT_DERIVED_ONLY_CAPABILITIES (voice.approve:<class>) — not
      clientApiId inputs. Serves #identity and #peer-link (G-ID-08 contract
      half).
    path: src/principal.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, identity, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/ids-principal-ref.test.ts

  contract-ref-v1:
    description: >-
      ref:v1 grammar (§4.4, §3.7, §3.9) — scheme ":" id ["@" rev]; kernel and
      package scheme lists, peer reserved (M1.1, P8-R9), voice dropped; aliases
      # $ ^ ! ~ → sym:, TD-/L-/T- → td:/l:/t:; parseRef, formatRef, peerRef
      (peer:<logId>/<ref>, never nested), validateRefV1, schemas/ref.v1.schema.json.
      Serves #ref-resolver.
    path: src/ref.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, ref-v1, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/ids-principal-ref.test.ts

  contract-refusal-v1:
    description: >-
      refusal:v1 Gnomon superset (§4.6) — P8-D89 (M1.4 slice 3) registers the
      read-token reasons (unknown-token, token-expired, token-revoked,
      token-in-use, token-not-yet-valid, token-store-untrusted), gone, the
      log.append ownership reasons (kernel-owned, ungranted, modns-not-own,
      bad-kind, bad-params), the slice-2 log.read / ref.resolve reasons
      (follow-needs-id, backlog-too-large, bad-since/until/limit/follow/kinds/
      scope, since-ahead, subscription-cap, mod-principal-name,
      reader-unsupported, bad-ref, rev-not-applicable, unknown-scheme,
      peer-ref, no-resolver, not-found, row-integrity, closed) and
      CLIENT_LOCAL_REFUSAL_REASONS
      (hello-not-offered); log.append's verb refusals gain ENGINE. copied (not imported) from
      packages/warpline/src/fabric/refusal.ts: Warpline's 12 codes + BUDGET_DENIED,
      PERMIT_REQUIRED, CAS_LOST, BILLING_REFUSED, MODEL_UNAVAILABLE; gates + budget,
      billing, model, voice, link, and reserved review, strictness (P8-D86–D88);
      Retriability; next[] steps; verdict and
      contested[].rule widened to string|null; optional additive data{reason,
      offered, cardId}; voice and link reason lists (M1.1); reserved
      review-cap, strictness-presence|paused|mode|evidence, voice-strictness,
      note-missing with RESERVED_REASON_ROUTES naming each one's code and gate;
      SOCKET_REASON_ROUTES for the reasons the M1.4 kernel socket emits; exit codes and the
      JSON-RPC code map (§4.9); refuse() single constructor, refusalOf()
      accessor (+ the JSON-RPC error depth), RefusedError, validateRefusalV1,
      schemas/refusal.v1.schema.json. G-CON-02 partial: every Warpline-shaped
      refusal validates. P8-D98 (T-2026-10-19-001): D98_REASON_ROUTES reserve
      CAS_LOST stale-claim | claim-expired | claim-superseded (§7.4),
      BAD_REQUEST cursor-epoch (§5 log.read) and ENGINE draining (§2.4 rule 11),
      all in REFUSAL_REASONS.
    path: src/refusal.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, refusal-v1, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/refusal-rpc.test.ts
      - test/contracts.test.ts
      - test/m1-1-reservations.test.ts

  contract-card-v1:
    description: >-
      card:v1 (§3.4, §14.7, §3.9) — P8-D98 (T-2026-10-19-001): kind
      daemon-stop (TD-2026-10-19-528 F3), CARD_EXPIRY_WHYS incl.
      session-drained (F4), decisionSig v2 layout (decisionMessageV2, first
      line DECISION_SIG_V2_MARKER gnomon:decision:v2, used for answer, carries
      the answer digest; the kernel signer adopts it in slice A2). Kinds incl. reserved voice-arm, grant,
      handoff, declassify, peer-pair, reconsider, strictness, incident; states
      incl. held; flags incl. voice-phrase, peer, irreversible, claim-mismatch;
      decisions incl. withdraw, extend, restart (reconsider cards only);
      fields note (change-note:v1, card form) and strictness{level L0-L3,
      mode manual|ask|auto-edits, reason} — level and mode ADDITIVE with
      fail-safe readings (unknown level ⇒ L3, mode ⇒ manual; no bypass mode);
      hasUnknownFailSafeValue ⇒ the card renders but is never decidable;
      strict producer checks: extend/restart (also as heldDecision) only on
      reconsider, claim-mismatch flag when agent tier < floor, irreversible
      flag when reversible:false (G-CHG-01/04); ROOT_CONFIG_RESERVED_SECTIONS; presence incl. voice-armed;
      via incl. voice, link; voice / voiceDecision blocks; signature domains
      gnomon:approve:v1 and gnomon:approve-voice:v1; CARD_RESERVED_VALUES;
      isCardDecidable (unknown state never decidable, held only withdraws);
      validateCardV1, schemas/card.v1.schema.json. Serves #approval-broker,
      ^voice-armed and ^peer-paired.
    path: src/card.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, card-v1, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/contracts.test.ts
      - test/m1-1-reservations.test.ts

  contract-gnomon-rpc-v1:
    description: >-
      gnomon-rpc:v1 (§4.9, §5, §12.3) — hello params/result types and
      validators, auth preimage helpers (authServerMessage / authClientMessage /
      authTokenMessage + their *Preimage forms, all binding the negotiated
      clientApi + canonical features; no unbound form; AUTH_TOKEN_DOMAIN
      gnomon:auth-token:v1 for read-token proof of possession — M1.4 slice 3,
      T-2026-10-17-017, P8-D89a); hello clientNonce (T-2026-10-18-016,
      P8-D93): HelloParams.clientNonce required (CLIENT_NONCE_PATTERN,
      base64url 22..86 chars, CLIENT_NONCE_BYTES = 32), echoed in
      HelloResult.clientNonce and bound into authServerMessage(nonce,
      clientNonce, endpointPath, negotiated) so a recorded hello cannot be
      replayed to another connection; client-local reason
      client-nonce-mismatch; negotiateHello (highest shared
      version, feature intersection, UNSUPPORTED{data:{offered[]}}); the frozen
      VERBS (12, with params, refusals and the §5 access matrix incl. the
      all-refused peer column; session.open runMode?, contract.claim note? /
      responses? + BAD_REQUEST, oracle.run FORBIDDEN per v3.9) and CLIENT_RELAYS
      (mod.view, mod.command); VERB_PARAM_VALUES, RESERVED_CONTENT_PARTS
      ({brief}), STATUS_RESERVED_FIELDS (links, strictness, review,
      unobservedRefWrites) and FAIL_SAFE_VALUES (in clientApiId);
      ADDITIVE_ENUMS + renderEnumValue implement the compatible-additive rule;
      schemas/gnomon-rpc.v1.hello.schema.json. P8-D98 (T-2026-10-19-001):
      HUMAN_DEVICE_VERBS gui.open{cwdHint?} (13) and rules.revoke{ruleId} (14)
      — human class only, access 'verified human device', every other class
      false; not among law 3's twelve kernel verbs; CLIENT_METHODS is 16;
      RESERVED_HELLO_FEATURES (journal.cursor, session.resume; the kernel
      advertises none until built); LogReadCursor {logId, seq} +
      validateLogReadCursor; D98_CLOSED_VALUES (always-rule match, drain
      reason); ADDITIVE_ENUMS gains approval.expire.why. Serves #socket and
      #web-endpoint.
    path: src/rpc.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, gnomon-rpc-v1, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/refusal-rpc.test.ts
      - test/m1-1-reservations.test.ts

  contract-client-api-id:
    description: >-
      kitId and clientApiId (§12.3, §12.8). TD-2026-10-19-063 (self-update
      pickup, founder ruling "ONE Touch ID", a deliberate move) moved
      clientApiId sha256:99d5c152…97d1 →
      sha256:ac22e72f26b673fae096b0495563c0c8029c8d37f9572526a1965b51eb0447e4
      (AUTH_WIRE_DESCRIPTOR gains `resume`: the {resumeToken} web form, the
      gui.resume notification, its TTL, single use, via 'resume' and its
      refusals). Before it, TD-2026-10-19-194 (voice V0,
      founder ruling, the one deliberate voice move before any client ships)
      moved clientApiId sha256:f27ecb8b…11a4 →
      sha256:99d5c1527bbbfadd7dca9cfa115e3fbaca227029cecd44c95843a86eb08197d1
      (descriptor gains voiceClosedValues = VOICE_CLOSED_VALUES:
      approval.voice.disarm.reason and refusal.voice-strictness.ceiling
      [null-level, manual]; statusFields gain arms, armCustody); kitId,
      modAbiId and abiId unchanged. P8-D98 (T-2026-10-19-001) moved
      clientApiId once (re-moved inside the same unreleased move for the
      drain-and-resume wire, Aegis M1, and once more for the #trace-capture
      wire, TD-2026-10-19-057 / Aegis M5: session.sandbox{traced, traceRefused}
      reserved, closedValues session.sandbox.traceRefused [trace-unsafe,
      trace-unavailable]): sha256:1faf47f5…8720 →
      sha256:f27ecb8b3ee5c1a4ad08d4c5eda427a63aebba8ba31963baed3c9d53e3e611a4
      (descriptor gains humanDeviceVerbs — gui.open, rules.revoke and, with
      TD-2026-10-19-339 inside the same unreleased move, daemon.stop{reason?}
      with closedValues daemon.stop.reason [stop, upgrade] — helloFeatures.reserved,
      logReadCursor, closedValues and DECISION_SIG_DESCRIPTOR — the decisionSig
      v2 marker gnomon:decision:v2, its decisions [answer] and one fixed
      message vector); kitId and modAbiId unchanged. P8-D93 moved clientApiId once
      (hello clientNonce + session.compacted): sha256:fd576e6d… →
      sha256:1faf47f5…8720 (round 2: server-sig domain v2, closed compaction-reason enum; round 3: AUTH_WIRE_DESCRIPTOR — the three auth domains and one fixed preimage vector per auth form — is a CLIENT_API_DESCRIPTOR input, so a domain or layout change moves the id); kitId unchanged. kitId = sha256(canonicalJson(kit:v1
      block list)); clientApiId = sha256(canonicalJson(CLIENT_API_DESCRIPTOR) +
      "\n" + kitId) where the descriptor = the 12 verbs + 2 relays, the JSON-RPC
      code map, ADDITIVE_ENUMS, every published client JSON Schema and the
      non-schema M1.1 reservations (verb param values, content parts, status
      fields); modAbiId
      is not an input. src/schemas.ts builds the schemas from the TS constants;
      schemas/client-api.ids.json pins the values per release.
    path: src/client-api.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, client-api, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/refusal-rpc.test.ts
      - test/contracts.test.ts
      - test/m1-1-reservations.test.ts

  contract-voice-allowlist:
    description: >-
      The voice allowlist (spec §14.7 "The allowlist", D58, D61, D62, D66;
      TD-2026-10-19-194, T-2026-10-19-026 voice slice V0) — pure data plus
      pure functions, the AUTHORITATIVE hand-only mechanism for #gnomon-voice
      decisions in $voice-approval under ^voice-armed: VOICE_CLASSES
      reversible ⊂ gate ⊂ judgment (cumulative, as the D62 grant sets);
      VOICE_ALLOWLIST, one frozen row per CardKind {approve{class →
      decisions it adds}, deny[]}: reversible = permission allow|deny,
      ask-user answer, plan approve-plan; gate adds gate-class allow,
      fallback fallback-cloud, budget resume; judgment adds knot resolve,
      verdict accept|reject; deny[] = the D66 row (each kind's deny-direction
      decision, deny or reject, under any class, no hold; founder ruling:
      incident and daemon-stop have EMPTY deny rows — fully hand-only). Default deny:
      anything not named (incl. every unknown kind or decision) is
      hand-only; any card flag refuses every decision but withdraw, deny
      included (voice-ineligible); flags is a REQUIRED argument (Aegis M1). voiceDecisionCheck(class, kind, decision, flags) →
      {ok, hold, via} | {ok:false, reason voice-off|voice-class|
      voice-hand-only|voice-ineligible} (all reserved in refusal.ts);
      voiceMayDecide is its boolean form; voiceApprovingDecisions;
      voiceAllowlistCoversCardKinds. withdraw (undo during the hold) is ok on
      any kind with an approving row at any class, never blocked by flags;
      the caller checks state held under the same armId. Also reserved here
      (event.ts/rpc.ts): the closed VOICE_DISARM_REASONS (21 values, incl.
      daemon-exit, helper-exit) and status.arms / status.armCustody. Callers pass the EFFECTIVE class; the
      strictness overlay, null-level ceiling, manual-mode deny-only clamp and
      every runtime broker check live in #approval-broker (later voice
      slices). Not a clientApiId input (pin unchanged; test/voice-golden.test.ts
      pins the clientApiId literal, packages/gnomon/test/voice-golden.test.ts
      the abiId literal and that every allowlisted pair is a valid
      KIND_DECISIONS pair in classes.ts).
    path: src/voice-allowlist.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, contracts, voice, paradigm-8]
    tests:
